@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
    ViewData["MetaDescription"] =
        "Meet Comfy Capy Calories, a friendly calorie and nutrition tracker built to make food logging easier.";
    ViewData["CanonicalUrl"] = "https://calories.comfycapy.com/About";
    ViewData["Robots"] = "index,follow";
}

<div class="content-page">
    <p class="page-eyebrow">About the app</p>
    <h1>Nutrition tracking, made a little comfier</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        Comfy Capy Calories is a calorie and nutrition tracker built around a simple idea:
        logging your food should be useful without becoming another chore.
    </p>

    <div class="content-card">
        <h2>What you can do</h2>
        <p>
            Set a personal calorie target, search UK and US food databases, create your own foods,
            track calories and macronutrients, and keep a daily Diary of what you've eaten.
            Saved Meals, familiar portions, approximate logging and Copy Previous Day help make
            the things you eat regularly quicker to log.
        </p>
        <p>
            Your Dashboard gives you a clear view of the day, while the Year Map lets you look
            back over the bigger picture without turning your food Diary into a wall of graphs
            and statistics.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-card">
        <h2>Why the Capy?</h2>
        <p>
            Nutrition tracking can be tedious, intimidating and, frankly, a bit boring.
            The Capy isn't. He is comfy.
        </p>
        <p>
            Comfy Capy is here to make the whole experience feel a little friendlier. You can
            customise your Capy, make him your own and have a tiny companion along for the ride.
            He won't judge what you had for dinner.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-card">
        <h2>Our design philosophy</h2>
        <p>
            We think the best tracker is the one you can actually be bothered to use. That's why
            Comfy Capy is built around reducing the little bits of friction that make food logging
            a pain in the capy.
        </p>
        <p>
            Exact measurements are there when you want them, but not knowing exactly how many
            grams were on your plate shouldn't stop you from logging at all. Features should have
            a clear reason to exist, information should be easy to understand, and the app should
            feel welcoming rather than clinical.
        </p>
        <p>
            In other words: keep the complicated stuff behind the scenes, keep the experience
            simple, and make it a little fun along the way.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3" role="note">
        Calorie targets and nutrition values are estimates for general information and tracking,
        not medical advice. Read the fuller
        <a asp-page="/Help" asp-fragment="nutrition-estimates">nutrition guidance</a>
        before relying on them for health decisions.
    </div>
</div>
